WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
1948.

2
00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:04.830
Migrants from the Caribbean
arrive in Britain.

3
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.680
Most of them are Christians.

4
00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.560
They join churches, and found new ones.

5
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:14.020
Today much church growth in
London is in migrant-led churches.

6
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:17.020
Then come migrants from
South Asia, East Africa,

7
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.080
West Africa and Europe.

8
00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:25.620
By the 2021 Census, 46.2 per cent in
England and Wales say they are Christian.

9
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.360
So how should Christians live with
neighbours who believe differently?

10
00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:34.380
In this mission, you'll trace how migration
made Britain a land of many faiths.

11
00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:39.950
Then you'll weigh up a hard question: should
Christians try to convert their neighbours?

12
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: find out how Christians might
live with neighbours who believe differently.
